    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d193-a1">

                <pb facs="0360" n="244" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg244"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 303.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to the conversation of
                    Wednesday last in which I laid before your excellency certain considerations in
                    regard to the prosecution in the Mixed Court at Shanghai of a certain Chinese
                    dealing in a product bearing an infringement of the vaseline trade-mark which is
                    the property of an American company, I have the honor to enclose herewith for
                    your consideration a memorandum setting forth the essential facts in the
                    case.</p>
                <p>I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paul Reinsch.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
